~/vm-bake/guest
# @summary The guests' views of the invoking user's home: VM_BAKE_VIEW_DIR/<guest> is one ZFS dataset per guest, which the guest mounts over virtio-9p as the whole home of its host-uid user when its template says 'service files view'. A leading ~/ is the invoking user's home. The parent is made once by root and delegated, so every ZFS act on a view runs without root: zfs create -o mountpoint=<this directory> <pool>/.../view, chown <user> on it, zfs allow <user> create,mount,snapshot,destroy -- 'guest view ensure' creates <parent>/<guest> below it and the mount point is inherited. What the guest writes there (its dotfiles, the state of its tools, its clones) lies in the home and is backed up with it; what it may see of the rest of the home is the template's home list, hung into the view by 'guest start' as nullfs overlays and let go by 'guest stop'.
